Hogwarts Legacy just confirmed new  gameplay details including a few that we  never expected in today's video I'll  break down my top 10 reveals from the  most recent gameplay showcase which  showed off the open world a more  detailed look at combat and a preview of  the room of requirement let's start off  with the brand new details on Broom  flight brooms will provide a quick way  to get around the open world outside of  Hogwarts as we ride there will be two  meters on the right side of the screen  the green being health and the yellow  being a boost meter according to game  director Alan 2 the higher you fly the  Broom the quicker this boost meter will  deplete of course because of the time  period we can't expect to ride anything  as Nimble and quick as Harry's Firebolt  for example in fact they've actually  Incorporated this into the story as  we'll be helping out a shopkeeper in  hogsmead who's trying to improve the  brooms they sell as we make upgrades our  broom will become faster and capable of  boosting even when we're higher in the  air we can also apply different cosmetic  changes to the broom through the same  shot it's also important to note that  the Cosmetics are purely that visual the  other upgrades will be handled  separately in addition to brooms we got  a more detailed look at how traversal on  a hippogriff or thestral works as well  the animal mounts will not have a boost  meter like the broom but can fly higher  right from the start without any penalty  they also have the advantage of quick  ground transportation in addition to  taking off for a quick flight around the  castle now it doesn't appear we'll be  able to cast spells while flying the  animal mounts or the broom however they  may still play a role in battle thanks  to a recent clip from the ccxp which  showed a grab horn trampling over some  goblins this showcase gave us an even  better look at the animations when we  summon these creatures from our  seemingly infinitely extendable bag that  would make Newt scamander proud the  animations have to be my favorite part  about all this rather than just having  these creatures fly beside us with a  whistle or some sort of spell we get  this incredibly slick animation that is  just perfect for this yet another small  way we're seeing Avalanche go above and  beyond to make this feel like an  authentic Wizarding World experience  when it comes to going above and beyond  though the room of requirement and  specific typically the customization  options have left many of us downright  stunned at all the options we have here  this is beautiful we never expected that  to be oh my God  gotta agree with my buddy Ben on that  one definitely one of those things we  were not expecting at all then you also  have this wonderful Conjuring effect  which looks like it came right out of  the movies now the dev team actually  refers to these as conjurations and they  also confirmed we'll be able to purchase  additional recipes for new furniture  from a shop called tomes and Scrolls  which is located in hogsmeade  additionally we'll unlock new objects by  engaging in different types of gameplay  throughout the world not only can you  conjure these items you can also scale  them larger or smaller and even change  the color the room of requirement is  also the area where we'll grow plants  and brew potions using these large  scientific tables which you guessed it  can also be customized one of the key  items located in the room of requirement  is this Enchanted Loom which is used to  upgrade gear and this brings us to yet  another big reveal from the Showcase and  that's the fact that we'll have three  different gear types legendary which is  orange extraordinary which is purple and  superb which is blue gear will  automatically include one primary  offense or defense stat but players can  use the loom home and magical materials  found throughout the world to add and  upgrade a secondary Stat or apply traits  to the Gear beasts can be rescued at  Beast dins whereas new trait recipes can  be collected in Bandit camps if you're  worried all these traits and gear will  mess with your ability to dress your  Witcher wizard in style Alan assures  players you can look like anything you  want whenever you want to you'll be able  to transmog gear so your preferred  traits and upgrades can apply to any of  your physical appearances now before  using the loom though you'll actually  need to conjure another item known as  the identification station this item is  used to identify new gear and reveal its  abilities so after that look at the  rumored requirement we were then traded  to a new look inside one of the game's  vivariums which is our area to care for  Magical beasts we've rescued from  poachers and if you thought we had a lot  of customization in the room of  requirement things open up even further  here systems designer McKenzie toner  referred to the conjuration items here  as ornaments many of them are purely  cosmetic but really help to create a  unique feel for the space that each  player will be able to make their own we  got a brief look at the potential here  with items like Stone archways ornate  benches and even feeders to speed up the  process of feeding the magical beasts to  keep them healthy and well fed oh and  there's also a toy box so you can play  fetch with the magical creatures now one  detail that was quickly skipped over in  the presentation but one that fans  absolutely caught right away is the  brief glimpse of a menu here that  reveals a braiding pin as one of the  options this will enable players to  conjure a pin that can be used to breed  two beasts and produce Offspring note  that the beasts we see throughout this  area all have an icon indicating whether  they are male or female yet another  gameplay mechanic here I don't think any  of us were expecting and it will be  fascinating to see just how deep this  mechanic goes how many different  creatures can we breed in here Community  manager Chandler wood even went as far  to say that what we saw in the Showcase  was only the tip of the iceberg for  everything you can do here so while I  know many weren't too happy about the  decisions to exclude quidditch and  minigames like Wizards chess for me at  least it's nice to see other mechanics  here like caring for magical creatures  and customizing our space in the room of  requirement as for some of the core  gameplay mechanics Alan mentioned there  are some items that are tied to the  game's day night cycle and while he  didn't explicitly confirm it I also  think this means it's likely we're  getting season specific and day night  specific quests as well in the first  part of the Showcase there were numerous  icons popping up around the world as the  player Flew Over the Hamlet surrounding  the castle missions that happen at  specific times of day certainly aren't  unique to Hogwarts Legacy and they've  been done in games before that being  said I'm so glad to see them here  because they always make the world feel  just a little bit more alive and a  little bit more believable as for the  seasons we also gotta look at what the  world outside Hogwarts looks like in the  snow and Alan even confirmed what's been  a big request from fans for quite some  time so there are moments like when it  reaches certain holidays or things like  that where hogs needs  holidays and the school reacts to  holidays and you see the decorations  around those environments change that  really helped just kind of make me feel  like I'm there one of the game's Biggest  Mysteries continues to be the ancient  magic in our character's connection to  it as far as The Story Goes we still  don't know much however we did learn  more in the Showcase about how this can  be used in battle as you chain combo  attacks against enemies and collect the  blue magical Aura Left Behind after some  fights you'll power up your ancient  magic meter once it reaches the halfway  point you'll be able to trigger an  incredibly powerful attack using L1 and  R1 in the Showcase we see this manifest  itself in three different attacks one  that has this sort of exploding effect  and we can kind of see some Sparks here  almost like a combustion and then  another one that just I don't even know  how you describe this just completely  makes the enemy disappears this sort of  black smokey effect and then one that  turns the enemy into a chicken according  to Alan the effect of this ancient magic  spell is actually dependent upon the  type of enemy we're fighting and the way  that manifests itself depends on the  type of enemy that you're fighting he  also confirmed the dash ability we  wondered about previously is an ancient  magic ability as well what he did not  confirm is what happens if we let the  meter fill all the way to the top is it  possible that would unlock the devastate  dating Lightning Spell we saw in a  previous trailer or maybe we just get  two of the ancient magic attacks that  we've already talked about they also  confirmed three battle arenas in the  game with two of them being available to  all players the dark arts battle arena  which they showed off in great detail  throughout the Showcase will only be  included in the deluxe and Collector's  Editions of the game or as an add-on  purchase for those who go with the  standard edition of the game Alan  mentioned these Arenas will pre-equip  players with certain spells so in the  case of the dark arts battle arena it's  all about the unforgivable curses now to  be clear anyone can unlock these curses  in the game whether you have the dark  arts pack or not but dark arts battle  arena will give you access to the  specific spells within the arena even if  you choose not to learn them in the main  game they also confirmed that you'll  earn different cosmetics by completing  the various battle arenas now as for the  three unforgivable spells we also  learned some key new details about them  first of which is the fact that they're  actually slottable spells and not simply  finisher spells that we had learned  about before also Avada Kedavra is true  to the series and completely takes out  enemies Wing cast does not matter even a  full-grown mountain troll gets taken  down with one shot now it does include a  longer cooldown meter to account for its  potency but what about the other  unforgivables well if you're curious  about those I have a full breakdown of  all three already posted here on the  channel so check out the video on the  right side of your screen now if you  want to learn just how devastating they  can be in Hogwarts Legacy as always  thank you all so much for watching I'll  talk to you again soon

